A [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] [[Gender|male]] operated as a member of the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] during the [[New Republic Era|era]] of the [[New Republic]]. Around [[9 ABY]], the '''bounty hunter''' was recruited alongside two other [[bounty hunter]]s by the Guild [[agent]] [[Greef Karga]], an agent of the Guild to steal a [[force-sensitive]] [[Din Grogu|Child]] from the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]], who had been tricked by Karga into thinking the agent was seeking the Mandalorian's help.

After meeting with Djarin and his own backup, the group set up camp for the night, only to be attacked by [[Nevarro reptavian|native reptavians]] which took away one of the [[Unidentified Trandoshan bounty hunter|bounty hunters]]. After the Child saved Karga's life, though, the agent had a change of mind. The next day, the Nikto and the other remaining [[Unidentified human bounty hunter (Nevarro)|bounty hunter]] attempted to kill Djarin when Karga chose to betray and kill the pair to help the Mandalorian.

==Biography==
===The meeting===
The [[Nikto]] was a [[bounty hunter]] in the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] on the [[planet]] [[Nevarro]]<ref name="Chapter 7" /> by circa [[9 ABY]].<ref name="Date" /> During that time, he was recruited by [[Greef Karga]],<ref name="Chapter 7" /> an [[agent]] in the Guild,<ref name="Greef Karga">{{Databank|greef-karga|Greef Karga}}</ref> to join his security detail. Along with a [[Unidentified Trandoshan bounty hunter|Trandoshan]] and a [[Unidentified human bounty hunter (Nevarro)|human]] [[bounty]] hunter, the Nikto accompanied Karga in meeting the [[Mandalorian]] bounty hunter [[Din Djarin]], who was in possession of a [[Force-sensitive]] [[Din Grogu|infant]] which the Guild had been hunting for an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|remnant]] of the [[Galactic Empire]]. Karga intended to kill Djarin and take the Child in order for the Imperial remnant to depart Nevarro.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

[[File:Karga_Aides_The_Mandalorian.png|thumb|left|280px|The Nikto accompanied Greef Karga alongside a Trandoshan and a human.]]
The Nikto joined Karga and the rest of his security detail in meeting Djarin in the [[lava fields]]. Karga had coaxed the Mandalorian there by convincing him that he intended to kill [[the Client]] from the Imperial remnant to make his forces leave. Djarin brought his own backup, the ex-[[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[shock trooper]] [[Carasynthia Dune|Cara Dune]] and the [[Ugnaught]] [[Kuiil]], all riding on [[Blurrg]]s. Karga acknowledged both of their security details and inspected the Child. The Nikto Djarin put their hands on their [[holster]]s, in order to draw [[blaster]]s if anything happened. Both of them relaxed their arms when the Child was put back into his pram.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

===The betrayal===
{{Quote|The plan was to kill you and take the kid. But after what happened last night, I couldn't go through with it.|Greef Karga on why he betrayed the Nikto|<ref name="Chapter 7" />}}
The two parties traveled across the [[Magma|lava]] fields before setting up camp for the night. At the camp, Karga discussed his "plan" to kill the Client with Djarin. However, he was attacked by a [[Nevarro reptavian|native reptavians]]. The group open fired as more of the creatures attacked the camp, taking away one of the Blurrgs. A moment of silence passed, until one of the creatures attacked the [[Trandoshan]] bounty hunter, carrying [[reptile]] away as the others shot at the animal. The group continued to fend off the creatures, losing another Blurrg in the process. After the flying animals left, Djarin and Dune tended to Karga, who had received a fatal wound from one of the creatures. Dune asked the Nikto and his human colleague if they had any medical supplies but they shook their heads. The Child then approached Karga and used [[Force healing]] on him, saving his life.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

[[File:NiktoHumanGunnedDown-TMCh7.png|thumb|right|280px|The Nikto and the human were killed by Karga, who had a change of heart.]]
The next [[Standard day|day]], the group approached the [[Nevarro City|city]] which the Imperial remnant had occupied. As Karga looked over to it with Djarin, Dune and Kuiil, he covertly signaled the Nikto and the human bounty hunter to shoot the latter three. The pair silently drew their blaster while behind Djarin and Dune. Karga, though, had had a change of heart after being healed by the Child. Abandoning his plan to kill Djarin and his colleagues, he swiftly drew his blasters and shot the Nikto and the human. The pair dropped to the floor dead, and Karga began revealing to Djarin and his backup of how he had intended to kill them.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

==Personality and traits==
The bounty hunter was a [[Kadas'sa'Nikto]] with [[Color|green]] skin with small brown areas and black [[eye]]s. He had his hand ready to draw a blaster during the time Greef Karga held the Child and relaxed when the Mandalorian did the same.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|Got any other med packs? Anyone?|Dune, to the Nikto and his colleague|<ref name="Chapter 7" />}}
The Nikto bounty hunter wore brown clothing with rusted [[armor]] protecting his torso and shoulders and an ammunition belt. He also donned a pair of black [[goggles]] and wielded a blaster which he kept in a brown [[leather]] holster.<ref name="Chapter 7" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Nikto bounty hunter first appeared in [[Chapter 7: The Reckoning|Chapter 7]] of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[2019]] television show ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'', which was directed by [[Deborah Chow]]<ref name="Chapter 7" /> and aired on [[December 18]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref>

